WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:04.710
Indium is a very soft metal. I haven’t got
a sample here. It

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:08.040
melts at 150 degrees or so.

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:11.370
This is an example of indium it is a really,
really quite nice

00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:14.450
chemical element this one. We can use it for
lots and lots of

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:18.250
selective types of catalysis, but generally
when it is forming a

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:21.690
complex with other organic ligands. But here
we can see a

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:26.210
really nice example of indium and this is
99.9% pure.

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:30.480
But it’s a metal which has suddenly become
very much more

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:35.649
expensive because its oxide is transparent
to light but will

00:00:35.649 --> 00:00:41.019
conduct electricity. So it is indium oxide
that you find on

00:00:41.019 --> 00:00:46.239
every LCD display. Here is a rather old computer
and here is

00:00:46.239 --> 00:00:50.030
an old fashioned computer, the LCD display
was quite small

00:00:50.030 --> 00:00:54.079
and gradually they have got bigger and bigger
and therefore

00:00:54.079 --> 00:00:58.889
demand for indium oxide is more and more and
probably you

00:00:58.889 --> 00:01:03.129
are watching this video clip through a thin
layer of indium

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:04.129
oxide.

00:01:04.129 --> 00:01:07.250
This sample although it’s very small, is
5 grams. So it is a

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:10.061
really, really, dense metal, very, very expensive
and very,

00:01:10.061 --> 00:01:11.560
very valuable as well.

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:17.380
But indium is also used as solder for soldering
various metals

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:22.310
together and it is also quite useful if, I
used it in my youth,

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:25.020
when we were making low temperature apparatus
and we

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:27.859
wanted to screw two things together and get
a nice seal in

00:01:27.859 --> 00:01:30.640
between them, you could screw them together
with a thin

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:35.759
sheet of indium, and that almost welded them
together.

00:01:35.759 --> 00:01:40.270
So indium wire; it is very, very malleable
and very, very soft

00:01:40.270 --> 00:01:43.649
and very easy to form into shapes. I am not
going to touch it

00:01:43.649 --> 00:01:46.380
though because it will cause some significant
problems for

00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:48.909
me, because it does cause toxicity if it comes
into contact

00:01:48.909 --> 00:01:51.610
with the skin; so lovely piece of indium wire.

